{"id": "EUVD-2026-103657", "enisaUuid": "620c3f29-dc0a-36b5-8180-9175b0ee7d3d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: usb: catc: bound the RX packet length in catc_rx_done()\n\ncatc_rx_done() walks a multi-packet URB, reading a two-byte length from\neach packet header. Its bound, pkt_len > urb->actual_length, ignores the\nheader offset and compares against the whole transfer rather than the\nbytes left from pkt_start, so a crafted packet header makes\nskb_copy_to_linear_data() read past the buffer.\n\nA length below ETH_HLEN is also accepted, including zero, and\neth_type_trans() then reads a MAC header from the uninitialised tailroom\nof a shorter skb. The is_f5u011 branch takes its length straight from\nthe transfer, so a zero-length URB reaches the same path.\n\nTrack the bytes remaining from the current packet, and reject a header\nthat does not fit, a length past what is left, and a length below an\nEthernet header.\n\nA transfer shorter than an Ethernet header, including a zero-length one,\npreviously became a runt skb passed to netif_rx() and counted as\nreceived; it is now counted in rx_length_errors and ends the walk.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3942557938f846e7481f6ccb2b41ccbdee61baa1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f87bbd5a7bf6ee79d598f7e22cf77810d29ae87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cc0a8eb2f9336cfa3e4ac329bc5585ca970ced3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21e206dd88b3de6e36bb607dec3797c59bc3007b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/801e21cf7dd6bcee31db907625d5045f21c9c1d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd9c6f8f05170223edec2dac476606cd40d9acb7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d4be026bdff2c1da7b6c7e01c0a47f2df409e97", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d565b6b72fe3f41fd43636e143072848105189f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xhrr-qp73-mj8c", "CVE-2026-98612"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08b8208a-3c7c-3558-8af5-3852f8cd6bba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3942557938f846e7481f6ccb2b41ccbdee61baa1"}, {"id": "10d64c01-eb5e-3174-b320-b5305f6c76e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "25632d67-b8c2-3bbb-a5ec-0ce5bb07633c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "380f3083-382b-3989-b754-5f1102f4f09e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "495ab73f-795e-3147-98d5-b78595abff9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "58b000df-4c1e-3a3d-bab9-44227a503298", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "5c985882-a874-35ed-b10e-39970fb1315e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "61eb9fb6-9a16-3b1e-91ba-50d1a0d02081", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "6bcb452d-eaa8-337f-b401-bb1d673d4e3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <21e206dd88b3de6e36bb607dec3797c59bc3007b"}, {"id": "830d4f51-5e62-3f24-8dc4-453ad582b4d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "83dab24d-1944-36ee-8d8f-e89823c42fe5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4cc0a8eb2f9336cfa3e4ac329bc5585ca970ced3"}, {"id": "97fd93ae-b8e1-328d-b48a-92c46d52378f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <dd9c6f8f05170223edec2dac476606